- [Hilary] I know, I know.

00:00:03.444 --> 00:00:05.250
- But I saved this,
this outfit is adorable.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.160
I love this outfit, it's so cute.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:07.993
- Thank you, thank you so much.

00:00:07.993 --> 00:00:10.292
Yes, it's... You know what?
I'm excited to get dressed up.

00:00:10.292 --> 00:00:11.125
- [Kelly] And it's been a minute,

00:00:11.125 --> 00:00:11.958
since we've seen each other.

00:00:11.958 --> 00:00:13.660
Oh yeah, do you not get?
Oh yeah, that's true.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.470
Because of the pandemic, people
don't usually do that yet.

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:16.930
Oh, I've been doing it for a minute.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.562
So, I'm excited still about PJs.

00:00:18.562 --> 00:00:19.395
(Hilary laughs)

00:00:19.395 --> 00:00:20.540
So, so it's good to see though,

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.400
but we're, we're coming
up on your third baby.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.330
You have three babies.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.470
- I do.
- It's a lot of work.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:26.690
And it's her first birthday? Is it?

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:28.830
- Yes, in March, she's turning one.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:29.663
I know.

00:00:29.663 --> 00:00:33.270
I actually, my son turned,
is turning 10 in March.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.990
I know double digits, I'm freaking out.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:36.373
So that's Mae-Mae.
- Look at that ponytail.

00:00:36.373 --> 00:00:38.020
- [Hilary] I know, we call her "Sticks".

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.788
Because like, her ponytail
just goes up in a stick.

00:00:39.788 --> 00:00:40.621
(audience laughs)

00:00:40.621 --> 00:00:41.454
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:00:41.454 --> 00:00:42.287
- [Hilary] That's Luca.

00:00:42.287 --> 00:00:43.120
- [Kelly] Oh, this is your 10 year old?

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:43.953
- [Hilary] Yes, and so,

00:00:43.953 --> 00:00:44.786
their birthdays are the 20th of March

00:00:44.786 --> 00:00:47.060
and the 25th of March.
(audience laughs)

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.470
Yeah, yeah, third baby,
you know, kind of thing.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.280
So, on his birthday I was just like,

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.113
"Don't come out, don't come out".

00:00:52.113 --> 00:00:53.797
- Oh yeah, you don't want
to have to share, yeah.

00:00:53.797 --> 00:00:55.400
- No, I know, but now I'm always going to

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.050
have to plan like, two
birthday parties in March.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.720
- Throw them together, yeah.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.553
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:01:00.553 --> 00:01:01.589
- I can't, one's 10, one's one.

00:01:01.589 --> 00:01:02.880
- I don't care.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:03.760
- I don't care.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:04.593
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:01:04.593 --> 00:01:05.589
- [Kelly] They'll be fine.

00:01:05.589 --> 00:01:09.370
But you've had a a home birth
for your second baby, right?

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:11.190
- For Banks, yeah, and for Mae.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.320
- [Kelly] So, for your second and third?

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.153
- Yes.

00:01:13.153 --> 00:01:13.986
- [Kelly] Was that, I
mean, was that like a...

00:01:13.986 --> 00:01:15.630
Because you had your
first one in the hospital.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:16.463
- [Hilary] Yeah.

00:01:16.463 --> 00:01:17.560
- [Kelly] And you had a
fine experience, probably.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.520
But what was the reason, why'd
you want to do home birth?

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:20.943
Because it kind of, terrifies me,

00:01:20.943 --> 00:01:22.600
because I had complications.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.600
So, you never know when you're
going to have complications.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.433
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:26.266
Well, you know what?

00:01:26.266 --> 00:01:28.420
I think that I had a
really easy first birth,

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.560
with Luca in the hospital.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.040
So I was kind of like, "All right,

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.260
I know my body can do this".

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.408
I didn't have any issues.
- Great body, okay yeah.

00:01:34.408 --> 00:01:35.499
(audience and Hilary laugh)

00:01:35.499 --> 00:01:37.740
My body was not that body.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.240
- You know what? Some people like aren't,

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.073
birthers like that, I don't know.

00:01:40.073 --> 00:01:41.100
- Yeah, my sister's like you.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.510
- My mom was like you.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:43.920
So, it's weird.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.900
I was very like, much
more comfortable doing it

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.398
in the hospital for the first time.

00:01:47.398 --> 00:01:48.231
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:48.231 --> 00:01:49.427
- And then I watched Ricky Lake's

00:01:49.427 --> 00:01:52.047
"The Business of Being
Born" and I was like,

00:01:52.047 --> 00:01:53.630
"I think I could do this,
I think I can do it".

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:54.830
- Wait, I missed that.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:56.728
So wait, it was just like
a home birthing video?

00:01:56.728 --> 00:01:57.848
- It's a home birth documentary.

00:01:57.848 --> 00:01:58.681
- Oh, I missed that.

00:01:58.681 --> 00:02:01.100
- You know what was really cool
about the home birth, Kelly?

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.270
Is like, you know, you're
bringing a baby into the world.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.200
That's some of the hardest
work that anybody can do.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.033
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:09.720
- And they don't let you have
like, water in the hospital

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:10.990
or food or snacks.

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:11.823
And you're about to like,

00:02:11.823 --> 00:02:13.540
work the hardest you've ever worked.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.820
To like, push a baby out.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.170
- So, at home you get all...

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.050
- Oh, I had sugar fish in bed,

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:19.328
I had a glass of rose afterwards.

00:02:19.328 --> 00:02:20.161
- You had sushi?

00:02:20.161 --> 00:02:23.970
- I had sushi in my bed with
my baby and a glass of rose

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.820
that I actually was like,
clawing at the bed to have.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.477
And I took a sip
afterwards and I was like,

00:02:28.477 --> 00:02:29.896
"Eh, this is not doing it for me".

00:02:29.896 --> 00:02:30.729
(audience laughs)

00:02:30.729 --> 00:02:32.100
But the day after I had some.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.330
- That's amazing, I'm so glad.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.640
That's such a cool experience too,

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:35.960
for like, your kids when they grow up.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.910
It's like, you are born at
home, that's so special.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:38.743
- You know what?

00:02:38.743 --> 00:02:40.830
It's kind of, the most
hippy-dippy thing about me.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.200
Like to have like, my kids
around while I'm birthing,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.320
Like, at first I thought
it was really weird,

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:46.610
but it was really beautiful

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:50.187
to like, bring another family
member in with everyone else.

00:02:50.187 --> 00:02:51.270
- I don't think it's very hippy-dippy,

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.670
I think it's self-sustaining.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.430
It's like, you can do
everything at your home.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:55.340
I think that's awesome.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:56.319
- You know what?

00:02:56.319 --> 00:02:57.470
One of my favorite memories was like,

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:00.610
Luca decided to sing Mae happy birthday.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.160
And I was like, I've never heard of anyone

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:06.360
singing happy birthday on a
first birth, like entering date.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.310
But he was like, "We should
sing her happy birthday".

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.728
And I was like, "Yeah, right".

00:03:09.728 --> 00:03:11.620
- I think that's so precious.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.453
I, here's the thing.

00:03:12.453 --> 00:03:13.460
- He's my sweet child.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.780
- I love, is that your oldest?

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:15.613
- Yes.

00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:16.710
- Okay, okay, okay.
(Hilary chuckles)

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.660
Okay, so after three kids,

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.130
are your friends coming to
you for a lot of advice?

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.260
Because I've actually had a
couple people on this couch,

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:23.790
say that they come to you for advice.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:25.750
Like you're like, a super mom.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:27.310
Like Mandy's one of them,
Mandy Moore was just here.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.910
- Mandy's the best,
she's also a super mom.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.200
So, you know what, I think,

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.070
just because I've been
doing this for 10 years

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:36.640
and a lot of my friends
just had babies, this year.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:39.900
So, I was obviously so excited for them.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:40.890
And then, you don't want to like,

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:43.970
take anyone's experience away, you know?

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:45.494
Like, everyone goes
through it differently.

00:03:45.494 --> 00:03:46.327
- Yeah, it's different.

00:03:46.327 --> 00:03:47.700
- I never wanted to be
like, mommy know it all,

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.010
but of course I love talking about kids.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:53.810
And so, I think the biggest
advice I would always give,

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.500
would just be like, don't get
fooled by the first two weeks,

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.120
because you have like, an angel baby

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.920
and they're just, they haven't woken yet.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:00.753
- Uh-huh.

00:04:00.753 --> 00:04:01.586
- [Hilary] You have those
friends that are like,

00:04:01.586 --> 00:04:02.960
"This baby is sleeping through the night.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.112
Oh, my God, it's already".

00:04:04.112 --> 00:04:04.945
(audience laughs)

00:04:04.945 --> 00:04:06.060
And I'm like, "they don't
know that they've entered

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:06.893
the world yet".

00:04:06.893 --> 00:04:08.520
- [Kelly] Or perhaps, the first year.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:09.860
You're like, "God, they're the kindest".

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:10.920
They eat everything, they do everything,

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:11.753
they're so nice.

00:04:11.753 --> 00:04:13.890
And then, it's just like...
(Kelly groans)

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:14.990
You're like, you're like,
"What is happening?"

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:15.823
- Oh yeah, my friend will be like,

00:04:15.823 --> 00:04:18.830
"My daughter's eating
curry and green things".

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:19.663
And you're like...

00:04:19.663 --> 00:04:20.624
- [Kelly] Enjoy it.
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:20.624 --> 00:04:21.722
- Wait, just wait.

00:04:21.722 --> 00:04:22.555
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:22.555 --> 00:04:23.650
Soon, it's going to be
like wiped off the...

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:24.503
- [Kelly] I hate this.

00:04:24.503 --> 00:04:25.336
- Yeah.

00:04:25.336 --> 00:04:26.685
- [Kelly] It's so weird.
(audience applauds)

00:04:26.685 --> 00:04:28.030
Her new show is called
"How I Met Your Father".

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.420
You can see it on Hulu

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.460
and it's just been renewed
for a second season.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:32.367
Congratulations.
(audience applauds)

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:33.200
- Thank you so much.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.033
- That's so awesome.

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:34.866
- Thank you.

00:04:34.866 --> 00:04:35.990
- [Kelly] So, you play Sophie,

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:39.620
who's explaining how she
met her son's father, right?

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:42.570
- Yeah, so it, you know,
it's a kind of like,

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:45.420
an extension of the "How
I Met Your Mother" show.

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:46.820
Because we're just, you
know, we're borrowing

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.870
how to tell that story
to your, your child.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.750
And in this case, Kim Catrall
plays the future Sophie,

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:54.130
which is so amazing.

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:55.140
- That's awesome.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.287
- I know, I love her
so much and she's just,

00:04:57.287 --> 00:05:00.360
watching her, I'm like,
"Sophie, made good choices,

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.470
she ended up okay".

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:03.140
Because like, this whole
adventure of the show

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.290
I think we're going to make her,

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.300
watch her not make perfect choices.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.600
And you know, she's
just like a young girl,

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:12.610
living in New York, who's 30
and trying to find herself

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:15.330
and find her footing and find true love.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.180
And she's like, really
holding onto the fact

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:19.257
that true love exists
and is out there for her.

00:05:19.257 --> 00:05:20.090
- Yeah.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.520
- You know, in the times of like,

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.860
everything being so
accessible and being swipeable

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:29.470
and endless options, it's a
really fun show to incorporate

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.530
like, what we're dealing with
in modern world right now.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:34.040
How fast everything is moving.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.020
- I know, I know, it's great.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.230
Well, speaking of meeting fathers,

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.520
so I've worked with your husband too.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.353
- I know.

00:05:39.353 --> 00:05:40.580
- So I, we were talking
about this backstage,

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.310
but I actually didn't know
that he was your husband.

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:44.550
I just missed that.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:46.370
And I was like, "Wait, what?"

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:49.550
And he wrote one of my favorite
songs called, "Someone".

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.020
It's on one of my albums and it's,

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.387
I've actually covered it on
here, as a Kelly classic.

00:05:52.387 --> 00:05:53.740
- I think you did, not too long ago.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:54.970
- [Kelly] I know, I love it.

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.390
It's literally one of my favorite songs.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:58.910
It's one of those songs
that people ask me,

00:05:58.910 --> 00:05:59.943
if you could've written
any of your songs, like,

00:05:59.943 --> 00:06:01.470
because I write a lot of mine,

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:02.470
but some of them I don't

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:04.038
and that's one of them that I'm like.

00:06:04.038 --> 00:06:04.871
- You wish you had written.

00:06:04.871 --> 00:06:05.704
- [Kelly] I wish I'd written.

00:06:05.704 --> 00:06:07.110
It's just so well done and it's fresh.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.310
And I think it's amazing because
you're an artist as well.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:10.460
You're a singer, songwriter as well.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.480
And I think that that's really cool,

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.130
that y'all, that worked.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:14.590
Like, sometimes the
artists marrying each other

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:16.201
doesn't work, I think that's so cool.

00:06:16.201 --> 00:06:17.034
(audience applauds)

00:06:17.034 --> 00:06:18.010
- He's never of complimented
one of my songs,

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.880
like he has your vocal on
your song, I'll just say that.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.420
- Okay.
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.240
I'm going to start fights now.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.510
No, but I just think that's awesome.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:26.343
Like, you're so artistic.

00:06:26.343 --> 00:06:28.620
Are your kids showing
signs of being so artistic?

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.080
Because you do like everything.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:30.920
- Yeah, oh thank you.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:33.690
Well, I try to do, I do some
things better than others,

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:34.523
but thank you.

00:06:34.523 --> 00:06:37.659
And it's, you know, we definitely
have a creative household.

00:06:37.659 --> 00:06:38.492
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:38.492 --> 00:06:40.200
- And Banks, I would say, my middle child,

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:44.200
is showing the most,
she's just a performer.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:47.760
Like, she is always performing
and it's really sweet,

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.190
but her style's real interesting.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.730
- Oh, that's going to
make the more fun kid.

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:52.706
I like that, okay yeah.

00:06:52.706 --> 00:06:54.070
- Usually she's nude, I'm like...

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:54.903
- [Kelly] Did you just say nude?

00:06:54.903 --> 00:06:55.736
- Nude.

00:06:55.736 --> 00:06:56.569
- That was me.
- Oh, well.

00:06:56.569 --> 00:06:57.672
- My Mom could not keep clothes on me.

00:06:57.672 --> 00:06:58.632
- If she could turn into you,

00:06:58.632 --> 00:07:00.141
I'm just going to let her keep going nude.

00:07:00.141 --> 00:07:01.880
- Well, you might want to start
her in therapy now, Hilary.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.880
(audience and Hilary laugh)

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:04.910
I'm just kidding, everyone needs therapy.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:06.581
- I agree, I agree.
(audience laughs)

00:07:06.581 --> 00:07:08.680
- No, but I, I just,
I didn't like clothes.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.220
I was like an exhibitionist
at a very young age.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:11.140
My mom would be so embarrassed,

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.140
I'd just take my clothes off.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:13.170
- Yeah, that...
- Anywhere.

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:14.291
- That is what she does too.

00:07:14.291 --> 00:07:15.771
I just, and you know what?

00:07:15.771 --> 00:07:18.180
We do the thing in our house,
we love to pants everybody.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:20.731
If you're walking by it's
fair game to just, you know.

00:07:20.731 --> 00:07:21.564
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:21.564 --> 00:07:22.520
If someones got a pair of sweatpants on.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:25.390
And so, Banks feels like
that's really normal.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:27.410
And I'm like, "Okay, we should stop some

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:29.752
of these antics because it's not normal".

00:07:29.752 --> 00:07:31.760
- So wait, my son loves, my
son loves to moon me right now.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.112
He just thinks it's so funny.

00:07:33.112 --> 00:07:34.020
- Because, you know what a pressed ham is?

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:34.853
- He's five.

00:07:34.853 --> 00:07:36.470
No, but he is five and he walks in

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.310
and he'll pull his
pants down, just perfect

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:40.000
to where you just see a little cheek,

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.264
like cheeks just like...

00:07:41.264 --> 00:07:42.310
- And you'll be like, on
a zoom call or something.

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:44.555
- And he'll turn around
and he'll be like "What?"

00:07:44.555 --> 00:07:45.388
(Hilary and audience laugh)

00:07:45.388 --> 00:07:47.510
And I'm like, it's kind of shows a little,

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:49.856
like a lot of personality.
(Hilary laughs)

00:07:49.856 --> 00:07:51.750
So, I should probably
tell him not to do it.

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:53.590
- A pressed ham is when you do that,

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:55.704
but you go put it on like a glass door.

00:07:55.704 --> 00:07:56.537
- Oh yeah, you press it?

00:07:56.537 --> 00:07:57.770
Oh, okay, I didn't know that was the name.

00:07:57.770 --> 00:07:58.747
- [Hilary] Yeah.

00:07:58.747 --> 00:07:59.580
My sister and I used to do it,

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.200
when we would drive from Texas to LA

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.683
and my mom would have no do no idea.

00:08:02.683 --> 00:08:04.634
We would do it in the
back seat of the car.

00:08:04.634 --> 00:08:05.467
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:08:05.467 --> 00:08:06.300
Those car rides are long,

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.973
two days, you've got to
like entertain yourself.

00:08:07.973 --> 00:08:09.243
- [Kelly] You've got...
And entertain the world.

00:08:09.243 --> 00:08:10.290
- I'm going to teach your kid
bad things if we ever meet.

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:12.530
- Yeah, apparently I allow
them to do them anyway.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:14.610
So, we're we're nailing motherhood.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:15.450
No, but who wins?

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:16.500
I want to ask, who wins in like,

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:17.680
a real life argument at your house?

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.780
Does one of you kind of
back off or are you good?

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:22.760
- So, he's a little too quick,
he's a writer, obviously.

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:24.810
You wanted to write that
song, he's a damn good writer.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.410
So, he works with words all day.

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:27.243
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:27.243 --> 00:08:28.076
- And then when we fight
and I've been like,

00:08:28.076 --> 00:08:30.802
dealing with children brains, I'm like...

00:08:30.802 --> 00:08:32.235
(Hilary mumbles)

00:08:32.235 --> 00:08:34.340
I can't like form the sentence
and he's like lashing.

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:35.173
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:35.173 --> 00:08:36.006
- And we don't really fight a lot,

00:08:36.006 --> 00:08:37.754
but when we do it can get
pretty heated, you know?

00:08:37.754 --> 00:08:38.587
- Yeah.

00:08:38.587 --> 00:08:41.930
- And so, he will have all
these phenomenal words to say

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:43.810
and just like, go in.

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:46.510
And I'll just be like
stunned for a second.

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:48.283
And if, and then I'll like hide his keys,

00:08:48.283 --> 00:08:49.453
because it'll make me feel...

00:08:49.453 --> 00:08:52.152
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:08:52.152 --> 00:08:52.985
- Oh, my God.

00:08:52.985 --> 00:08:54.464
- Wow, she's a little crazy.

00:08:54.464 --> 00:08:56.243
- I actually love you.

00:08:56.243 --> 00:08:57.076
(audience applauds)

00:08:57.076 --> 00:08:58.380
- One time, one time his phone was like,

00:08:58.380 --> 00:08:59.784
sitting on the couch
and I was just like...

00:08:59.784 --> 00:09:00.617
(Hilary groans)

00:09:00.617 --> 00:09:01.940
And he like, wow, stormed out of the room.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.104
And I just slipped it in the couch.

00:09:04.104 --> 00:09:07.120
(audience and Kelly applaud)

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:09.100
- Oh my God, I love you.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:11.900
I'm going to start, I might
start doing that on my kids,

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.872
just to mess with them
when they're disrespectful.

00:09:13.872 --> 00:09:15.450
(Kelly and Hilary laugh)

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.272
It was so lovely to see you.

00:09:17.272 --> 00:09:18.105
- [Hilary] Oh my gosh.

00:09:18.105 --> 00:09:19.243
- I love hanging with
you, you're such a...

00:09:19.243 --> 00:09:20.076
(audience applauds)

00:09:20.076 --> 00:09:20.909
- I love hanging with
you, I love your show.

00:09:20.909 --> 00:09:21.742
- A great guest.

00:09:21.742 --> 00:09:22.575
- I have to tell you,

00:09:22.575 --> 00:09:24.853
when Fran, I call her
Fran, Fran from the show.

00:09:24.853 --> 00:09:27.580
Francia, when she came
on I was so jealous.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.150
I was like, "I haven't even been on".

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:30.792
- [Kelly] Wait, we've
been talking about this.

00:09:30.792 --> 00:09:31.625
- How'd you get on?

00:09:31.625 --> 00:09:32.460
- Wait, I'm so glad you
brought it up though,

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:35.680
because she brought me
hot sauce and she made it.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:36.513
- Yeah.

00:09:36.513 --> 00:09:37.346
- [Kelly] It's amazing.

00:09:37.346 --> 00:09:38.179
- I know.

00:09:38.179 --> 00:09:39.012
- [Kelly] Have you had it?

00:09:39.012 --> 00:09:39.845
- Yeah and when she comes over to my house

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:41.010
and she doesn't bring it,
I'm like, "Why did you come?"

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:41.843
- [Kelly] Rude.

00:09:41.843 --> 00:09:42.676
- Yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:09:42.676 --> 00:09:43.509
Don't you know the arrangement here?

00:09:43.509 --> 00:09:44.457
- You can't show people that, yeah.

00:09:44.457 --> 00:09:46.300
- I know and we want to sell it so bad.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:47.133
I want to call it...

00:09:47.133 --> 00:09:48.047
- You should sell it.

00:09:48.047 --> 00:09:48.880
- Francia's Salsia.

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:50.760
- No, I'm telling you she should sell it.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.240
I've literally been
talking about that salsa

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:53.073
since she left.

00:09:53.073 --> 00:09:55.900
- I know, but she's really
being like, very difficult

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:58.250
about trying to just
supplement fresh cilantro

00:09:58.250 --> 00:09:59.580
for like, dried cilantro.

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:01.841
I'm like, just try it so we
can see if we can bottle the...

00:10:01.841 --> 00:10:02.674
(beeping)

00:10:02.674 --> 00:10:03.507
(Kelly laughs)

00:10:03.507 --> 00:10:04.340
- Sorry...
(beeping)

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:06.360
(Kelly laughs)

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:08.010
- No, but it is, it's an amazing salsa.

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:10.190
Y'all should do that,
that's a very smart idea.

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:11.887
All right, everybody new episodes of

00:10:11.887 --> 00:10:14.487
"How I Met Your Father"
drop every Tuesday, on Hulu.

